<manifest xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">

    <!--
      Phase 0 spike hooks (spec section 15). Confined to the debug source set so a release
      build never contains them.

      SpikeActivity is exported so `adb shell am start -n com.oru/com.oru.radio.SpikeActivity`
      can launch it as the visible component that legalizes starting the microphone
      foreground service from the command line.

      SpikeReceiver IS exported. The original assumption here — that `adb shell am broadcast`
      (running as the shell UID, 2000) can reach a non-exported receiver on a debug build —
      does not hold on every device/OS version: some (confirmed on Android 16 / ColorOS)
      reject it with a Permission Denial ("is not exported from uid ..."), which silently
      breaks every ptt-* command sent from adb. Since this whole surface only ships in debug
      builds and disappears from release, exported="true" is an acceptable trade to keep it
      actually reachable from adb everywhere.

      The launcher used to be aliased to SpikeActivity because debug builds had no RN UI yet.
      The real screens exist now, so the launcher and com.oru.MainActivity resolve to the
      normal RN activity again (inherited unmodified from the main manifest); SpikeActivity
      and SpikeReceiver stay reachable by explicit component name for the adb-driven flows in
      docs/phase0-android-spike-hooks.md.
    -->
    <application>
        <activity
            android:name="com.oru.radio.SpikeActivity"
            android:label="Oru Spike"
            android:exported="true" />

        <receiver
            android:name="com.oru.radio.SpikeReceiver"
            android:exported="true" />
    </application>

</manifest>
